# rpg_pvp_hq_blueprint.phases.pdl - PROGRAM rpg-pvp-hq BY BLUEPRINT, then play it (BOOK 16.game/EVENT-VERB-PAGES-DESIGN.md section 10). Same idea as game_dev_hq_blueprint.phases.pdl.
# Runner: ops/+x/playthrough_op.+x run play/phases/rpg_pvp_hq_blueprint.phases.pdl   (scratch house under /tmp; nothing live is touched)
GAME | rpg-pvp-hq | rpg_pvp_hq
EVENTS | yes
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/dec_op.+x

PHASE | p1_buy | the shop button plays the buy page and one bed is bought | blueprint, buy, fire
DO | status
DO | fire | buy | bed_blue
HAS | state/fire_log.txt | buy\ppage:bed_blue | the-buy-page-was-played
COUNT | state/house.txt | BUY\p | 1 | one-purchase

PHASE | p2_reprogram | edit the buy page in the blueprint so its command is scavenge; the same shop button now finds a rag and buys nothing | blueprint, edit, scavenge
BP | buy | edit | 1 | rpg_pvp_hq_verb | verb=scavenge\parg=
EXIT | 0 | blueprint-edit-applied-by-the-manager
DO | fire | buy | bed_orange
HAS | state/fire_log.txt | buy\ppage:bed_orange | edited-page-was-played
COUNT | state/house.txt | BUY\p | 1 | no-second-purchase
HAS | state/events.txt | give_item\p | the-rag-scavenge-ran

PHASE | p3_restore | edit it back and the shop buys again | blueprint, edit, buy
BP | buy | edit | 1 | rpg_pvp_hq_verb | verb=buy\parg=
EXIT | 0 | blueprint-edit-back-applied
DO | fire | buy | bed_orange
COUNT | state/house.txt | BUY\p | 2 | the-shop-buys-again
